From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BiSheng <raft-mobile-bisheng@mail.build>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 11:35:39 +0000
Subject: feat(compose): lower PathEffect dashes to the canvas lineDash command

The vendored DrawScope kept every pathEffect parameter commented out, so a
Compose Canvas could not draw a dashed line even though every renderer's
CanvasView already implements lineDash. Restore the Jetpack Compose surface
(PathEffect.dashPathEffect, Stroke.pathEffect, Paint.pathEffect, the
pathEffect parameters of drawLine/drawPoints) and lower it in KuiklyCanvas:
a DashPathEffect becomes lineDash(intervals / density), a null effect sends
an empty lineDash, and the sticky native dash state is only re-sent when it
changes or after the canvas is rebound (reset).

drawLine now also honors the paint's stroke cap, like fillOrStroke does.
Only the dash effect is supported; phase is accepted for source
compatibility and ignored because no renderer exposes it.

Fork-Patch: compose-canvas-path-effect-dash
Upstream-Status: pending

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: BiSheng <raft-mobile-bisheng@mail.build>

